  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1231 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nToday through Thursday night...The surface ridge will shift east \nof the area this afternoon the flow will become more \nsoutheasterly. Highs will be in the mid 50s across most of the\narea. Southerly flow will increase out ahead over another \nfront/short wave on Saturday with warmer highs in the mid/upper \n60s. The boundary will sweep across the area on Sunday, but it \nlooks like moisture/instability will be limited. Will have to\ncontinue to monitor this, but no outlooks are expected at this \ntime. Expect mostly scattered showers/storms Sunday afternoon \ninto the evening hours. \n\nHigh pressure will build across the area on Monday and continue \ninto Wednesday, but a the models are indicating a stronger storm\nsystem on Thursday./15/",
